          "title": "You'll want to know: гипотеза",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "гипотеза (gipóteza) — \"a hypothesis\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Учёные проверили эту гипотезу. Uchyónyye provérili étu gipótezu. The scientists tested this hypothesis."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. Выдвинуть гипотезу — to put forward a hypothesis."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "гипотеза (gipóteza) comes from Latin hypothesis, from Greek hypóthesis \"the basis of an argument, a supposition\" (EtymDB), built from hypó \"under\" and thésis \"a placing\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
